Offline PMP report-layout comparison: J714s/T6050 and public T6040/T6041 support
J714s source: cached runtime ADT from docs/research/probe-logs/t6050-cpu-impl-0100-2026-11-04-j714s.log
Public reference: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/linux/pull/374
Reference file: drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c, apple_pmp_offsets_t6041
No new hardware reads, serial connection, PMP start, or register writes.

J714s PTD range entries: 29
Field                  J714s byte offset  T6041 byte offset  Match
PMP-STATUS read         0x000010           0x000010           True
SOC-DEV-PS-REQ read     0x001e00           0x001e00           True
SOC-DEV-PS-ACK read     0x001e80           0x001e80           True
FAST-DIE-CE read        0x002580           0x002580           True
SOC-DEV-PS-REQ write    0x010f00           0x010f00           True

ADT records are decoded as 32-byte <IIII16s entries.
Read offset = entry offset * 16; write offset = 0x10000 + entry offset * 8.
The comparison establishes these offsets only, not the meaning of every field,
MMIO access permissions or widths, matching firmware protocols, or PMP startup.
The public M4 startup code still writes ASC CPU_CONTROL; T6050 ASC access remains
a reported obstacle in https://github.com/omacom/linux-aurora/issues/293.
